hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24072","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed to us Mamar, he said: al-Zuhri said: And Umar ibn Thabit al-Ansari informed me that some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day to the people, while warning them of the trial of al-Dajjal: You know that none of you will see his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, until he dies, and it is written between his eyes: disbeliever. Whoever hates his deed will read it."
